id: pm-linear-canonical-terminal-states
title: Map Linear canonical canceled and duplicate state types to closed
description: Published Linear GraphQL WorkflowState.type includes canceled and duplicate. The existing mapper recognized cancelled but treated both canonical terminal types as open. Negotiation must report the same correct terminal mapping that sync applies.
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: changed,linear,schema
created_at: "2026-10-22T15:36:04.749Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T15:54:18.852Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Canonical canceled and duplicate state types map to closed; cancelled compatibility spelling remains supported
comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T15:37:41.025Z",codex-agent,"No matching issue found in canceled/duplicate state searches. Linear published GraphQL schema documents canceled and duplicate as terminal workflow type values. The shared mapper now maps those types to closed and also recognizes Canceled in the name fallback, retaining cancelled compatibility. Added three regressions: 3/3 pass; reverting only mapStatus to the base function makes all 3 fail, restoring makes 3/3 pass. Typecheck, test typecheck and docstring lint pass. Schema versions now also hash resolved mappings so future mapping-algorithm changes invalidate old plans. Parent context: pm-linear-schema-drift."
  "2026-10-22T15:54:16.735Z",codex-agent,"Implementation fully verified in PR 163, CI run 39807792715 at 4a6758f8e4170ce51e6dfb71b8ca8a7370dd5f7d: npm and Bun release gates each passed 323/323 tests with zero failures; Node 22/26 jobs passed too. Canonical terminal regressions passed 3/3 through pm test --run --progress, and reverting only mapStatus failed all 3 before restoration. No SDK/core behavior was forked: negotiation uses the shared importer mapper and runtime status registry. Claim released for orchestrator verification; not closed."
